   rejects, so converting it would revive a dropped declaration (lightningcss: translate) */.t12{transform:translateX(var(--x))}/*! declined: a \`/*!\` banner is kept, as cssnano, csso and clean-css also do (lightningcss drops it) */.t13{color:red}/*! declined: merging rules that share a block reorders the cascade (csso, cssnano) */.t14{color:red}.t15{color:red}/*! declined: not identical, so the first is a fallback for an engine that cannot
   read the second — dropping it is how esbuild and lightningcss lose this pair
