to\` is what the \`none\` keyword means */.t25{flex:none}/*! flex: \`1 1 auto\` is what the \`auto\` keyword means */.t26{flex:auto}/*! flex: names match case-insensitively */.t27{FLEX:none}/*! flex: already a keyword */.t28{flex:none}/*! declined: \`flex:1\` means \`1 1 0%\`, and a length \`0\` is not a percentage \`0%\` */.t29{flex:1 1 0}/*! declined: the same shorthand spelled with \`0%\` — collapsing it needs the one-value form's defaults */.t30{flex:1 1 0%}/*! declined: a prefixed property is a different property */.t31{-webkit-box-flex:0 0 auto}/*! declined: \`attr()\` substitutes a token sequence too, through its fallback */.t35{margin:attr(data-m type(<length>),1px 2px 3px) attr(data-m type(<length>),1px 2px 3px)}/*! declined: the same for \`if()\` */.t36{margin:if(style(--x: 1): 1px 2px 3px;else: 4px) if(style(--x: 1): 1px 2px 3px;else: 4px)}/*! declined: ...and \`inherit()\`, which substitutes a custom property's whole value */.t37{margin:inherit(--gap) inherit(--gap)}/*! declined: ...and \`first-valid()\` */.t38{margin:first-valid(1px 2px 3px) first-valid(1px 2px 3px)}/*! a function only ending in a substitution's name is a different function */.t39{margin:myvar(1px)}/*! declined: only \`border-radius\` takes a second box, so a \`/\` elsewhere is invalid — collapsing it would switch the declaration on */.t32{margin:1px 1px/1px 1px}/*! declined: the same for a property whose one box would otherwise collapse */.t33{padding:2px/2px}/*! declined: ...and for a keyword box */.t34{border-width:1px/1px}/*! declined: a CSS-wide keyword is only valid as the whole value, so the repeated form is already discarded */.t40{margin:inherit inherit}/*! declined: the same for the other four */.t41{padding:unset unset}/*! declined: ...and the \`/\` box is no way around it */.t42{border-radius:revert revert / revert revert}/*! \`auto\` is a per-side value, not a CSS-wide keyword */.t43{margin:auto}/*! merge-longhand: four sides become the shorthand */.t44{margin:1px 2px}/*! merge-longhand: ...in whatever order they were written */.t45{margin:1px 2px}/*! merge-longhand: ...and the \`{1,4}\` collapse still applies */.t46{padding:0}/*! merge-longhand: \`inset\`'s longhands are the bare side names */.t47{inset:1px 2px 3px 4px}/*! merge-longhand: border-color, border-style and border-width all qualify */.t48{border-color:red}/*! merge-longhand: a component may be a function */.t49{margin:3px 2px 1px}/*! merge-longhand: inside an at-rule too */@media (width>=1px){.t50{margin:1px 2px}}/*! declined: an incomplete family is not the shorthand */.t51{margin-top:1px;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:1px}/*! declined: \`!important\` must agree across the four */.t52{margin-top:1px!important;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:1px;margin-left:2px}/*! merge-longhand: ...and does when all four carry it */.t53{margin:1px 2px!important}/*! declined: a substitution could expand to more than one component */.t54{margin-top:var(--x);margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:1px;margin-left:2px}/*! declined: a CSS-wide keyword is only valid as the whole value */.t55{margin-top:inherit;margin-right:inherit;margin-bottom:inherit;margin-left:inherit}/*! declined: a longhand holding two components is already invalid */.t56{margin-top:1px 2px;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:1px;margin-left:2px}/*! declined: a repeated longhand makes the cascade decide, not the order */.t57{margin-top:1px;margin-top:3px;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:1px;margin-left:2px}/*! declined: something between the four writes the same family, so the merge would move it */.t57b{margin-top:1px;margin-inline-start:9px;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:3px;margin-left:4px}/*! declined: ...and a vendor prefix does not hide that — Chromium reads \`-webkit-margin-start\` */.t57c{margin-top:1px;-webkit-margin-start:9px;margin-right:2px;margin-bottom:3px;margin-left:4px}/*! merge-longhand: an unrelated property between them is free to move */.t57d{margin:1px 2px 3px 4px;color:red}/*! declined: \`all\` writes every family